+
+### Bounded external resource-free SPIR-V stages
+
+`DeviceProfile::import_resource_free_spirv` accepts an immutable `ExternalSpirvStage`
+(`pipeline::external_spirv`). It returns the ordinary opaque `CompiledFunction` for
+`StageSource::Compiled`; the existing pipeline linker and binding planner stay in use.
+The existing AIR compiler remains the default and is unchanged.
+
+This experimental import is a strict subset: SPIR-V 1.5, `main`, 32-bit straight-line
+vertex-index/position or resource-free float4 color0 fragment stages. Its bounded typed
+validator checks IDs, instruction order, linear control flow, operands, stores and the
+complete declared interface. It refuses descriptors, push constants, specialization,
+vertex attributes, varyings, other outputs and unknown instructions. The fragment's
+location is a real linker relocation. Attachment conversions that require compiler
+lowering still refuse through the ordinary `ColorWrites` contract; importing does not
+claim the conversion happened. No runtime compiler provider selects this path yet.
+
+Facts bind the profile and little-endian word digest, plus nonzero source-AIR and
+producer identities, into a separate semantics-versioned compile key. Those last two
+identities are caller provenance, not an attestation of AIR/SPIR-V semantic equivalence;
+the producer remains trusted for translation semantics. There is no caller-supplied
+cache key, resource layout, reflection or unknown precision claim. External tools run
+only in tests, never on the library path. Callers must impose the normal isolated-worker
+20-second/500-MiB budget around the external compiler and validator.
